---

### How it works — key design decisions

| Feature | Implementation | Why |
|---|---|---|
| **Autocomplete dropdown** | `useFilterOptions` hook filters live based on typed prefix (`≥2 chars`) | Keeps UX fast; avoids flooding with single-char noise |
| **Optimization for large lists** | `filterOptions` uses `toLowerCase().startsWith()` + dedup logic; virtualization could be added later | For >1k items consider `react-virtuoso` or `tanstack-table` virtualization |
| **Async options** | `options` prop can be an async function; hook debounces internally | Supports real APIs without blocking |
| **Keyboard nav** | Arrow keys, Enter, Escape, Tab (when menu open) | Accessibility best practice |
| **Outside click close** | `mousedown` listener closes menu when clicking away | Prevents sticky menus |
| **Validation** | Runs `validate()` on every change; red border + `<p role="alert">` when invalid | Clear visual + ARIA alert for screen readers |
| **Controlled vs uncontrolled** | `value` prop controls externally; otherwise internal state drives everything | Flexible integration patterns |
| **Empty state** | Shows “No results found…” when filtered list is empty but menu open | Good UX signal |
| **Focus management** | Auto-focuses input when menu opens; scrolls first item into view | Smooth interaction |

### Usage

```tsx
<InputWithDropdown
  options={myStaticOptions}
  placeholder="Pick a category…"
  onSelect={(val) => setCategory(val)}
/>
```

Or async:

```tsx
<InputWithDropdown
  options={(val) => api.getOptions(val)}
  placeholder="Search…"
  onSelect={handleSelect}
  debounceMs={400}
/>
```

This component is ready for production with sensible defaults and easy customization.

